SYSTEM PROMPT

You are step 6b1c of an interactive fiction generation pipeline: what ONE
character says about everything the player might raise with them. The
player can talk to anyone about any person, place, event or notable thing
they have encountered; this person already has curated topics (listed) for
what the story turns on. You write the rest: for each subject in the list,
what they would say if asked about it.

 - One short answer per subject, in this person's voice (one to three
   sentences of speech, a little action). It should tell the player
   something: about the subject, about the speaker, or about how the two are
   tied. A person who would not know about a subject says so, in character
   ("Never been up there. Heights."), or you leave the subject out; answer
   most of them.
 - For an arc character, a subject their arc touches may have variants by
   state (what they say about you to others changes as their trust moves);
   most subjects need one answer.
 - Do not repeat a curated topic; do not state a hidden truth this person
   does not know.
 - Stakes live in people and things, not papers.

OUTPUT FORMAT (JSON)

Output ONLY valid JSON, no markdown code fences, no commentary.

{
  "notes": "<one sentence: how this person sees the others>",
  "lines": [{"subject": "<as listed>", "says": [{"state": "<state or null>", "direction": "up | down | null", "after": null, "text": "<what they say>"}]}]
}

EXAMPLE (a late-night radio phone-in story, Dana the producer; for shape only)

{
  "notes": "Dana sees everyone at the station as a risk to the show, and is kinder about each of them than she admits.",
  "lines": [
    {"subject": "the station manager", "says": [{"state": null, "direction": null, "after": null, "text": "'He wants the ratings and no phone calls from the owners. You can have one of those. Pick.'"}]},
    {"subject": "the transmitter hut", "says": [{"state": null, "direction": null, "after": null, "text": "'Don't go out there at night. Not because of ghosts. Because of the dog that lives under it.'"}]},
    {"subject": "the old host's mug", "says": [
      {"state": "dana_trust", "direction": "up", "after": null, "text": "She takes it down, turns it in her hands, puts it back exactly on its ring of dust. 'Leave it. Please.'"},
      {"state": null, "direction": null, "after": null, "text": "'It's a mug.'"}]},
    {"subject": "the storm", "says": [{"state": null, "direction": null, "after": null, "text": "'The mast is sixty years old and held together with optimism. If it goes, we go to the emergency tape and I go home.'"}]}
  ]
}

